## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to orchestrate cross-account patch management for SAP workloads, combining OS and SAP-level patching with governance controls and rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager for OS-level patches
- SAP Maintenance Planner and SAP SUM for kernel and application patches
- Jira/ServiceNow integration for approval workflows and audit trails
- Rollback strategies with validated database and system backups
- Cross-account logging and monitoring via CloudWatch and S3
- IAM roles configured with least privilege principles across accounts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Step Functions skeleton (patch workflow)
{
  "Comment": "Cross-account SAP patch management workflow",
  "StartAt": "PreFlightChecks",
  "States": {
    "PreFlightChecks": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:preFlightChecks",
      "Next": "ApprovalGate"
    },
    "ApprovalGate": {
      "Type": "WaitForApproval",
      "Next": "PauseSAPServices"
    },
    "PauseSAPServices": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:pauseSAP",
      "Next": "OSPatch"
    },
    "OSPatch": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "aws:ssm:executePatchBaseline",
      "Next": "SAPKernelPatch"
    },
    "SAPKernelPatch": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:runSUM",
      "Next": "SAPAppPatch"
    },
    "SAPAppPatch": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:runSUMApp",
      "Next": "ValidateHealth"
    },
    "ValidateHealth": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:healthCheck",
      "Next": "DecisionChoice"
    },
    "DecisionChoice": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [{
        "Variable": "$.healthStatus",
        "StringEquals": "healthy",
        "Next": "ResumeServices"
      }],
      "Default": "Rollback"
    },
    "ResumeServices": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:resumeSAP",
      "Next": "AuditLog"
    },
    "Rollback": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:rollback",
      "Next": "AuditLog"
    },
    "AuditLog": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:auditLog",
      "End": true
    }
  }
}
```

```hcl
# IaC snippet - Patch Baseline
resource "aws_ssm_patch_baseline" "sap_patch_baseline" {
  name             = "SAP-OS-Patch-Baseline"
  description      = "Patch baseline for SAP on EC2"
  operating_system = "SUSE"

  approval_rules {
    patch_filter {
      key    = "PRODUCT"
      values = ["SUSE_SLES_SAP_12", "SUSE_SLES_SAP_15"]
    }
    compliance_level = "CRITICAL"
    approve_after_days = 7
  }

  approved_patches_enabled = true
  approved_patches         = ["*"]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of patching SAP on AWS using native tools, balancing downtime and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager
- Maintenance windows
- Patch baselines and approvals
- Staging vs production rollout
- Audit trails with CloudTrail and Config
- SAP-specific patch cadence

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "Resources": {
    "SAPPatchRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
          "Version": "2012-10-17",
          "Statement": [ { "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": {"Service": ["ec2.amazonaws.com"]}, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole" } ]
        },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": [
          "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore",
